        "not ok 44 - catalog entries carry via on the wire under a new tag while the old tag keeps its shape",
        "not ok 48 - migrate-state-2 carries the repositories forward and defaults the queue empty",
        "not ok 49 - migrate-state-3 rewrites every stored repository without a group policy",
        "not ok 51 - on-load migrates zero through three forward while accepting four",
        "not ok 66 - peer pull wire and receive state carry selected refs",
        "not ok 67 - peer pull API validates selected refs and offers both to the origin",
        "not ok 72 - merge advances only the recorded target ref and gates Clay only for that ref",
        "not ok 73 - pull summary and detail JSON expose sourceRef and targetRef",
        "not ok 77 - native peer browse responses hide repository administration fields",
        "not ok 81 - outgoing offers remain active until authoritative state is consumed",
        "not ok 88 - raw-object streaming adds a new begin packet and authenticated self packets",
        "not ok 89 - transfer-id capability negotiation preserves the legacy request wire and pack fallback",
        "not ok 90 - transfer modes and stream jobs are transient and reset on init and load",
        "not ok 92 - object page v2 uses a list of bounded fragments instead of a map",
        "not ok 93 - batch helpers enforce one-MiB fragments and one-MiB pages lazily",
        "not ok 94 - stream preparation stores an object job and schedules its first event without pre-growing",
        "not ok 95 - each stream-next builds and grows exactly one bounded fragment list then yields",
        "not ok 96 - stream-grown advances the job and announces begin-objects only after page one",
        "not ok 97 - begin-objects mirrors begin validation, selects object mode, and fills the receive window",
        "not ok 98 - pack begin remains sequential and explicitly preserves pack mode",
        "not ok 99 - Fine molds object fragment lists while retaining the exact pack fallback",
        "not ok 100 - release, snapshot failure, supersede, and serve timeout delete stream jobs",
        "not ok 101 - stream handlers no-op if either their job or object serving flight disappeared",
        "not ok 102 - both Fine modes reuse peer-snapshot OID validation and atomic finish",
        "not ok 103 - fragment pages reject malformed bounds and duplicate oid/offset pairs before accounting",
        "not ok 104 - zero-length Git objects use one metadata-only fragment and remain content-addressed",
